The flakiness in this test is caused by a race condition or concurrent access to the `outputParams` map. The mock server may handle requests using a thread pool, or multiple requests (such as redirects or pre-flight requests) might hit the handler concurrently. Since `HashMap` is not thread-safe, concurrent writes can corrupt its internal structure, leading to lost updates or `null` returns when calling `get()`. 

Changing the data structure to a thread-safe `ConcurrentHashMap` resolves the concurrency issue and ensures deterministic test execution.

//<import start>
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
//<import end>

