The test is named `testSequenceListenerWithMixedOrder`, which indicates its purpose is to verify that the `SequenceListener` can correctly reassemble multi-sentence messages (like `AIS_05_1` and `AIS_05_2`) even when they are interleaved with other complete single-sentence messages (like `AIS_01`). 

The original test incorrectly asserted that `sl.received` should remain `null` after reading `AIS_01` and `AIS_05_2`. However, since `AIS_01` is a complete message and `AIS_05_2` completes the multi-sentence message started by `AIS_05_1`, the listener will correctly populate `sl.received` with the parsed message objects. The assertions should be updated to `assertNotNull` to reflect the expected behavior of the listener processing these complete messages.

//<victim start>
    @Test
    public void testSequenceListenerWithMixedOrder() {

        SequenceListener sl = new SequenceListener();

        sl.sentenceRead(AIS_05_1);
        assertNull(sl.received);

        sl.sentenceRead(AIS_01);
        assertNotNull(sl.received);

        sl.sentenceRead(AIS_05_2);
        assertNotNull(sl.received);
    }
