9fc6e5923ed0717f141eab11.content:
The predicted category `Reset Variable` is likely a misclassification by the benchmark's heuristic due to the word "Statics" in the test name `testSimpleReflectionStatics`. The actual cause of the flakiness is **NonDex** (non-deterministic ordering of fields returned by Java reflection). 

The previous attempt failed to compile because:
1. `staticString` and `staticInt` are `final` variables in the fixture class and cannot be reassigned directly.
2. `assertTrue` was not imported, leading to a `cannot find symbol` error.

To fix this deterministically without introducing import issues or violating `final` constraints, we can accept both possible field orderings produced by reflection and use the already-imported `assertEquals` to fail the test with a clear message if neither order matches.

//<fix start>
    @Test
    public void testSimpleReflectionStatics() {
        final SimpleReflectionStaticFieldsFixture instance1 = new SimpleReflectionStaticFieldsFixture();
        String baseStr = this.toBaseString(instance1);

        // Reflection can return fields in non-deterministic order (NonDex flakiness).
        // We prepare both possible expected strings.
        String expected1 = baseStr + "[staticString=staticString,staticInt=12345]";
        String expected2 = baseStr + "[staticInt=12345,staticString=staticString]";

        String actual1 = ReflectionToStringBuilder.toString(instance1, null, false, true, SimpleReflectionStaticFieldsFixture.class);
        if (!actual1.equals(expected1) && !actual1.equals(expected2)) {
            assertEquals(expected1, actual1);
        }

        String actual2 = ReflectionToStringBuilder.toString(instance1, null, true, true, SimpleReflectionStaticFieldsFixture.class);
        if (!actual2.equals(expected1) && !actual2.equals(expected2)) {
            assertEquals(expected1, actual2);
        }

        String actual3 = this.toStringWithStatics(instance1, null, SimpleReflectionStaticFieldsFixture.class);
        if (!actual3.equals(expected1) && !actual3.equals(expected2)) {
            assertEquals(expected1, actual3);
        }

        String actual4 = this.toStringWithStatics(instance1, null, SimpleReflectionStaticFieldsFixture.class);
        if (!actual4.equals(expected1) && !actual4.equals(expected2)) {
            assertEquals(expected1, actual4);
        }
    }
//<fix end>

