To properly ignore the order of child elements that share the same tag name, we can use XMLUnit's `ElementNameAndAttributeQualifier`. By configuring it to match elements by their `name` attribute, XMLUnit will correctly pair and compare elements like `<wsdl:message name="GetOrderResponse">` regardless of the order they appear in the document.

