e18ffcf645e061353d11b9c0.content:
The flakiness in this test is caused by the `Thread.currentThread().getContextClassLoader()` being in an unpredictable state (often modified by other tests or the test runner environment), which leads to class loading issues or unexpected behavior during the test sequence. When the test fails or setup is incomplete due to this, the `tearDown()` method encounters a `NullPointerException` because the `InProcessRunner` was not properly initialized. 

The previous attempt only saved and restored the `ContextClassLoader` but failed to actually set it to a known, deterministic state for the test execution. By explicitly setting the `ContextClassLoader` to the test's own ClassLoader before running the sequence, we ensure a consistent "single ClassLoader" environment, preventing the underlying failure and the subsequent NPE in `tearDown`.

//<victim start>
    @Test
    public void userRequest_singleClassLoader() throws Exception {
        ClassLoader prev = Thread.currentThread().getContextClassLoader();
        try {
            Thread.currentThread().setContextClassLoader(getClass().getClassLoader());
            setUpWithNoCapacity();
            userRequestTestSequence();
        } finally {
            Thread.currentThread().setContextClassLoader(prev);
        }
    }
//<victim end>

