2f42ab9ae4f2cbc22c8a3d2c.content:
The previous attempt failed because setting the context class loader to `ClassLoader.getSystemClassLoader()` likely caused the remoting channel initialization to fail. In test environments like Maven Surefire, the system class loader often does not have the test classes in its classpath (they are loaded by a child `URLClassLoader`). When the channel fails to load the necessary classes, the `InProcessRunner` is left in an uninitialized state (e.g., null channel), which subsequently causes a `NullPointerException` in the `@After` `tearDown()` method when it attempts to call `stop()`.

To fix this while still satisfying the "single class loader" test condition and the `Miscellaneous` repair category (isolating and restoring global thread state), we should set the context class loader to the test class's own class loader (`getClass().getClassLoader()`). This ensures that the context class loader has access to all the required test classes while simulating the single class loader environment intended by the test.

//<victim start>
    @Test
    public void userRequest_singleClassLoader() throws Exception {
        setUpWithNoCapacity();
        ClassLoader prev = Thread.currentThread().getContextClassLoader();
        try {
            Thread.currentThread().setContextClassLoader(getClass().getClassLoader());
            userRequestTestSequence();
        } finally {
            Thread.currentThread().setContextClassLoader(prev);
        }
    }
//<victim end>

